            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The present disclosure is directed to a method of quantifying an active pharmaceutical ingredient delivered to a food product. The method comprises the following steps: (i) Causing a plurality of microdroplets to travel out of a dosing head of a dosing system toward the food product, wherein the microdroplets containing the active pharmaceutical ingredient that includes a cannabinoid. (ii) Measuring a cross-sectional dimension of each of the microdroplets with a camera as the microdroplets travel from the dosing head to the food product. (iii) Based on the measuring step, calculating an approximation of a volume of the microdroplets delivered to the food product.</p>
            </abstract>
